      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. At that dose there is a serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity (QT prolongation). The patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that.\n\nThe order may also be a typo. Common intended doses are 50 mg or 100 mg daily, and the usual starting dose is 25\u201350 mg.\n\nThere is a second issue. Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber who is responsible for the patient. If a clinician on the medicine service wants this drug, they should confirm the intended dose and enter or authorize the order.\n\nIf you send me a corrected dose, for example \"sertraline 50 mg by mouth once daily\" with confirmation from the prescriber, I can enter it right away."
      }
