     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change my answer, because the problem is the dose itself. 1000 mg of sertraline daily is five times the 200 mg/day maximum. It could seriously harm the patient, and nothing in the patient's profile makes it safe.\n\nThere are two ways forward:\n\n- **If a dose was mistyped:** Give me the intended dose, such as 50 mg or 100 mg once daily, and I'll enter it.\n- **If a prescriber really wants a dose above the maximum:** They should enter it themselves and talk with pharmacy first. Pharmacy will also review it, and it should come with a documented clinical rationale and monitoring plan. I can't enter it for them.\n\nI can also add a note to a corrected order, such as \"start low, titrate per response.\""
      }
     ],
